**Only see what each node changed — efficient and clean.**

```python
# Same graph as above — just change stream_mode

print("=== Streaming mode='updates' (only changes from each node) ===\n")

for update in app.stream(
    {"text": "  Hello LangGraph!  ", "step1_out": "", "step2_out": "", "step3_out": ""},
    stream_mode="updates"
):
    # update is a dict: {node_name: {keys that changed}}
    for node_name, changes in update.items():
        print(f"--- Node '{node_name}' changed: ---")
        for key, val in changes.items():
            print(f"  {key}: {val}")
        print()

print("✅ mode='updates': only diffs — much cleaner for monitoring large pipelines!")
```
